see my grand evil design here
im going to make it hallucinate the entire interface log based on what's in the context. and have it naturally correct it's prediction as 
real interface data comes in, more it matches, it gets tagged as a positive fact, those which do not match, gets tagged as negative fact.

the challenges i know is, what topic to create the hallucination on, like how likely would it able to share the topic of a potential conversation in the real interface?
it is easy when context is small, but if it had talked to users on many topics, then it would need to know what topic to hallucinate about. 
sure i can pick the last discussed topic and store it when user revisits that topic again.

the llm will get the context, on what that log is
or we can have a different vron running in idle, to compare it against stored interface logs.